  "contents": [{
    "heading": "overview",
    "content": "Fumadocs MDX refined its API surface for better cross-framework compatibility and flexibility."
  }, {
    "heading": "plugins-api",
    "content": "We introduced Plugins API, enabling extensible modifications to MDX configurations without bundler-specific code—ideal for file generation (e.g., types, indexes) or config alterations."
  }, {
    "heading": "plugins-api",
    "content": "There's a json-schema plugin natively provided by Fumadocs MDX."
  }, {
    "heading": "nextjs",
    "content": "createMDXSource and resolveFiles are now relocated to fumadocs-mdx/runtime/next."
  }, {
    "heading": "nextjs",
    "content": "This should not affect majority of projects, as docs.toFumadocsSource() is now the preferred way."
  }, {
    "heading": "vite",
    "content": "The source.generated.ts file is now moved to .source/index.ts, you are recommended to import the .source folder (with a path alias)."
  }, {
    "heading": "vite",
    "content": "Migrate:"
  }, {
    "heading": "vite",
    "content": "run dev server/typegen to generate a .source folder."
  }, {
    "heading": "vite",
    "content": "import it over the original source.generated.ts."
  }, {
    "heading": "vite",
    "content": "note that both docs and create-fumadocs-app are updated to .source folder."
  }, {
    "heading": "vite",
    "content": "We also supported index file generation targeting other runtimes like Bun/Node.js."
  }, {
    "heading": "bug-fixes",
    "content": "remark-include: fix Markdown stringify logics."
  }, {
    "heading": "bug-fixes",
    "content": "postprocess.includeMDAST support."
  }, {
    "heading": "bug-fixes",
    "content": "(Vite) support useContent on client loader for lint avoidance."
